menu "Reproducer configuration"

config REPRO_WIFI_SSID
    string "Wi-Fi SSID"
    default "myssid"
    help
        The co-processor joins this network. The sender (send_bulk.py) must be on it too.

config REPRO_WIFI_PASSWORD
    string "Wi-Fi password"
    default "mypassword"

config REPRO_TARGET_DMA_FREE_KB
    int "Leave this much DMA-capable internal memory free (KB)"
    default 24
    range 8 128
    help
        The program holds INTERNAL|DMA memory until only this much is free, which is what makes a
        full streaming read fail to allocate. A full read is (co-processor SDIO Tx queue size) *
        1536 B; with the default queue size of 20 that is 30720 B, so 24 KB reproduces the fault
        quickly. Raise it to confirm the healthy case: with enough of this pool free, the same
        traffic runs indefinitely.

endmenu
